<body>
<header><h1>📜 Computer Science Timeline</h1><p>Explore selected milestones in computing.</p></header>
<main>
<article class="event"><div class="year">1830s</div><h2>Analytical Engine Concept</h2><p>Charles Babbage designed a concept for a general-purpose mechanical computing machine.</p></article>
<article class="event"><div class="year">1940s</div><h2>Electronic Computers</h2><p>Electronic digital computers developed rapidly during this decade.</p></article>
<article class="event"><div class="year">1950s–1960s</div><h2>Programming Languages</h2><p>High-level languages such as FORTRAN and COBOL helped make programming more accessible.</p></article>
<article class="event"><div class="year">1970s</div><h2>Microprocessors</h2><p>Microprocessor technology helped pave the way for smaller computers.</p></article>
<article class="event"><div class="year">1980s</div><h2>Personal Computing</h2><p>Personal computers became increasingly common in homes, schools and workplaces.</p></article>
<article class="event"><div class="year">1990s</div><h2>The World Wide Web</h2><p>The Web expanded access to linked information and online services.</p></article>
<article class="event"><div class="year">2000s–Today</div><h2>Mobile, Cloud and AI</h2><p>Mobile computing, cloud platforms and artificial intelligence continue to influence daily life.</p></article>
</main>
